extraction_notes: |
  - category occ / occ_group psychic per the batch convention (modelled on
    mind-melter), although the book heads it "Psi-Slayer R.C.C." (printed 69)
    and "Psi-Slayer Psychic R.C.C." (printed 73). men_of_arms false: a Master
    Psionic class under a psychic R.C.C. heading, with no hit point or S.D.C.
    formula printed.
  - Race restrictions (printed 73): "Humans only", stored as only ["none"],
    the reserved human case - it permits humans and forbids pairing with any
    D-bee/R.C.C. race. The lore (printed 70) also calls them human.
  - xp_table taken from the brief (read off a render of printed 157).
  - Psionics (printed 73, ability 2): seven powers granted outright; the
    powers_starting 8 are two each from Healing, Sensitive, Physical and Mind
    Bleeder. Level 2 gives no powers but a one-of-five bonus choice (a
    special_abilities entry; not applied automatically - the schema has no
    chosen-bonus mechanism). Level 3: two from Sensitive/Physical/Healing plus
    one from Super or Mind Bleeder. Levels 4-15: "a total of two powers from
    Healing, Sensitive or Physical, OR one from the Super-Psionic category".
    Judgement call: the schedule cannot express an either/or, so each level
    grants two from Healing/Sensitive/Physical (the strict reading) and the
    note offers the Super trade for the GM to arbitrate; including Super in the
    gate would have allowed two Supers per level, which the book does not.
  - The four exclusive powers (Sleepwalk, Locate & Track Mark, Telekinetic Air
    Walk, Psi-Dagger; printed 71-73) are not psionic_powers catalog rows; the
    character picks any two. Stored as special_abilities with their stats; the
    pick-two rule is not enforced. Candidate catalog rows for a later PR.
  - I.S.P. (ability 3): 2D4x10 + M.E., +10 per level. The cache reads
    "2D4xlO" (known digit fault = 2D4x10). P.P.E. (ability 4): 2D6+4.
  - Bonuses (ability 5): +1D6+12 S.D.C. as pools.sdc; +1 P.E.; +1 roll with
    punch; +4 horror factor; +2 vs mind control drugs stored as
    saves.mind_control; +2 vs possession; +1 initiative at levels 1, 3, 5, 7,
    9, 11 and 13. +1D6 to pull punch is a dice value, which a combat bonus
    cannot hold - special_abilities entry. Master psychic save at 10+ is prose.
  - P.P.E. vampire feeding and starvation rules (ability 1, printed 73) are
    conditional and are special_abilities entries, not bonuses.
  - Skills (printed 74): "Spoken Languages: Choose Two" - no separate native
    tongue line is printed, so none is granted (same call as psi-nullifier).
    Fixed skills fold the printed bonus into the catalog base (Interrogation
    30+15=45; Streetwise 20+8=28). "Basic Math" is Mathematics: Basic;
    "Tracking" is Tracking (people); "General Athletics" is Athletics
    (general). Hand to Hand: Martial Arts, "or Assassin, if evil" with no
    price - costs { assassin: 0 }.
  - Related skills: the book misprints "P.C.C. Related Skills". Five at level
    one, two more at 3, 6, 9 and 12. Military is "None" unless the character
    was trained by a military organization such as the CS Psi-Battalion (then
    any, +5%); left out of the categories and stated in the note. Secondary:
    four, no later additions printed.
  - Equipment (printed 74): "black jump suit" stored as clothing;
    "camouflage clothing" as camouflage-fatigues; "300 ft/91.5 m of durable
    rope" as 8 x rope (40 ft each = 320 ft); "climbing & rappelling gear" as
    climbing-kit plus full-rappelling-equipment; "walkie-talkie with secure
    capability" as walkie-talkie; "IRMSS" as the full IRMSS row. NOT stored:
    "1D4+1 sets of fake identification" (no gear row), "some personal items",
    and "military fatigues and dress uniform (only if part of an organized
    service)". "Four extra ammo clips for each" pistol and rifle stored as 8
    e-clips. Energy weapons are enumerated from generic rows; the book allows
    CS, Triax, NE or even TW models. Vehicle: none to start.
  - Money (printed 74): 4D6x1000 credits (cache "4D6xlOOO", digit fault) plus
    Black Market items worth 2D6x1000 credits, which starting_money cannot
    hold. The book adds that even rookies earn 2-3 times a mercenary''s wage.
  - Alignment: any, mostly Anarchist (25%), Miscreant (25%) or Diabolic (20%).
    Attribute requirements M.E. and P.P. 12 or higher (stored); high physical
    attributes and good I.Q. helpful. Cybernetics: avoids implants; bionic
    prosthetics/organs only if absolutely necessary, bio-systems preferred.
---

## Lore

Psi-Slayers - also called Psi-Killers or Psi-Assassins - are human master psychics taken young by secret assassins'' guilds and shaped into hunters of people rather than into Mind Melters. They work as spies, bounty hunters and killers, specialize in hunting other psychics, and are counted among the deadliest humans on Rifts Earth, perhaps second only to the Sunaj. Like the Psi-Stalker they feed on the P.P.E. of their prey, and most relish taking it at the moment of a kill. Most are selfish or evil, though a minority serve as lawmen and heroes, and every one of them finds the call of vengeance nearly impossible to resist. They are restless drifters who favor the Magic Zone, Tolkeen, Free Quebec, the Great Lakes, the Pecos Empire and the New West, and they are about a third as common as Mind Melters.

## GM Notes

**Power selection by level** (Psyscape p.73):

- **1st level:** Psychic Body Field, Detect Psionics, Sense Magic, Sixth Sense, Intuitive Combat, Mask I.S.P. & Psionics and Mind Block automatically, plus two powers each from Healing, Sensitive, Physical and Mind Bleeder, plus any two of the four exclusive powers.
- **2nd level:** no powers; choose one bonus (+1D4 M.E., +1D4+1 M.A., +3 initiative, +1 attack per melee, or +2D6+2 permanent I.S.P.).
- **3rd level:** two powers total from Sensitive, Physical and/or Healing, and one from Super or Mind Bleeder.
- **4th level and up:** two powers total from Healing, Sensitive or Physical, or one Super-Psionic power instead. The app offers the two; trade them for a Super pick by hand.

**Wild-territory worldview:** Psi-Slayers respect and fear experienced Tattooed Men, Mind Melters, Temporal Raiders and shapechangers (they loathe the last), and treat most other opponents as rivals or prey. They like Psi-Stalkers, Dog Boys and Simvan as associates.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'psi-slayer');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'psi-slayer';

